  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nI just found this very old  [Mozilla bug](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=974212) by @jruderman that shows that serializing (and reparsing) comments is not safe.\n\n```javascript\nvar comment = document.createComment(\"--><img src=/ onerror=alert('xss')><!--\");\ndocument.body.appendChild(comment);\ndocument.body.innerHTML += \" \";\n```\n\nFollowing the work in #6235 to fix a similar problem for attributes, this seems like a lower stakes issue that we should consider fixing.",
